SCREENSHOT(1)               User Commands              SCREENSHOT(1)

NAME
    screenshot - save the screen as a PNG file

SYNOPSIS
    screenshot [-d seconds] [file]

DESCRIPTION
    screenshot copies the screen from the display server at the device
    resolution and writes it to file. Without file, the image is written
    to $HOME/Pictures/screenshot-DATE-TIME.png. The Print Screen key
    starts screenshot without arguments.

OPTIONS
    -d seconds   wait before the copy

    The path of the written file is printed on standard output.

EXAMPLES
    screenshot
    screenshot -d 5 /home/desktop.png

SEE ALSO
    gzip(1)
